<title>USA: Weekend U.S. box office chart -- Oct 25-27.</title>
<headline>Weekend U.S. box office chart -- Oct 25-27.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the final data for the top 10 movies at the October 25-27 U.S. box office, according to Exhibitor Relations Co.</p>
<p>    Film		    Three-day gross    Cumulative Gross</p>
<p> 1. Sleepers		    $9,606,059	 $ 26,351,436</p>
<p> 2. High School High	  $6,311,786	 $  ----</p>
<p> 3. Stephen King's Thinner  $5,679,046	 $  ----</p>
<p> 4. The Ghost and the</p>
<p>    Darkness		    $4,390,078	 $ 26,792,125</p>
<p> 5. The First Wives Club    $4,380,111	 $ 88,693,006</p>
<p> 6. The Associate	     $4,261,304	 $  ----</p>
<p> 7. The Long Kiss Goodnight $3,673,909	 $ 25,305,313</p>
<p> 8. Michael Collins	   $2,409,761	 $  2,941,151</p>
<p> 9. That Thing You Do!	$2,050,606	 $ 20,554,737</p>
<p>10. D3: The Mighty Ducks    $1,655,851	 $ 18,214,445</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;Sleepers&quot; and &quot;Michael Collins&quot; are released by Time Warner Inc.'s Warner Bros. &quot;High School High&quot; is released by Sony Corp's TriStar Pictures. &quot;Stephen King's Thinner&quot;, &quot;The First Wives Club&quot; and &quot;The Ghost and the Darkness&quot; are released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc..  </p>
<p>&quot;The Associate&quot; and &quot;D3: The Mighty Ducks&quot; are released by Walt Disney Co. &quot;The Long Kiss Goodnight&quot; is released by New Line Cinema, a unit of Time Warner's Turner Broadcasting System. &quot;That Thing You Do!&quot; is released by News Corp.'s 20th Century Fox.</p>
